Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 16:18:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests/stacking: Sync with the X server before comparing
 stacks

Some tests such as workspace-maximized and map-after-headless are
flacky as failing when comparing the xserver stacking.

In fact test_case_check_xserver_stacking() compares the results of
XQueryTree() with the stack tracker contents, which is updated via
the X events the display has received.

A client that just created or restacked a window can show up on the X
side before we have handled the corresponding event, so the X server
list may mismatch the mutter one.

So wait the events being handled before doing the comparison.
---
 src/tests/test-runner.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/tests/test-runner.c b/src/tests/test-runner.c
index bb42f3c5d68..04ae2dc77c3 100644
--- a/src/tests/test-runner.c
+++ b/src/tests/test-runner.c
@@ -438,6 +438,9 @@ test_case_check_xserver_stacking (TestCase *test,
   if (!display->x11_display)
     return TRUE;
 
+  if (!test_case_wait (test, error))
+    return FALSE;
+
   guint64 *windows;
   int n_windows;
   meta_stack_tracker_get_stack (display->stack_tracker, &windows, &n_windows);
